{
  "$note": "How each generated network is drawn: the tile colour (`bg`, a CSS colour or gradient), whether the mark and the name are dark (`dark`, for a light tile), and where its mark comes from (`mark.src`) and how it is drawn (`mark.mode`). Read by scripts/update-networks.ts; the fifteen hand-placed networks in networks-curated.json are not here. Sources: `w3:` web3icons raw-svgs (MIT), `hl:` hyperlane-registry chains/<name>/logo.svg (MIT), `el:` ethereum-lists/chains _data/icons/<name>.json via IPFS (MIT; submitted by each chain's team), `site:` the network's own website, `copy:` another network's mark already in public/chains. Modes: `mono` — a white mark, turned near-black on a light tile; `white` — every colour in the SVG becomes white (near-black on a light tile); `asis` — the SVG as published; `raster-white` — a transparent raster turned into a white (or near-black) silhouette; `raster` — the raster as published, resized; `round` crops it to a rounded square, for icons that are a filled square of their own. Colours come from the marks themselves (the web3icons `background` variant, the dominant fill of the official mark, the solid field of a square icon) or from the brand's own site; a brand that is black and white gets a black tile, the way Robinhood and Plasma have one.",
